>Anyway, I cleared out the castle and amongst other things I wished for a 
>blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail, and received a black mantelet which is +
>3 and did very good things for my AC.  I worked up from lvl 50 and found 
>the Wizard on lvl 43.  I can kill him, but he always gets me with his 
>finger of death, and even if I survive the first battle it is usually at 
>the cost of my amulet of life saving.  He then gets me next time which is 
>soon after.
>
>I was under the impression that +3 GDSM gave anti-magic protection.  Was I 
>wrong?  Should I have wished for a cloak of magic resistance?

You got me.  GDSM *does* protect from magic, including finger-of-death.
That spell shouldn't be killing you.  (Unless you're not *wearing* the GDSM.)
I know that this sounds silly, but are you sure that :

1) you're wearing the GDSM?  It won't work if it's merely in your inventory.
2) it's *gray* dragon scale mail?  Other color dragon scale mail gives
   different resistances.  (Red dragon -> fire resistance, etc.)

BTW, I don't think that these are spoilers.  These are parameters of the
game.  To win, someone needs to tell you that you need to level teleport
into Hell to find the Wizard. (Well, usually.)  Anyone who wants to win
the game should be told that that artifacts exist, and that dragon scale
mail can be created.

